From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:41 -0500
Subject: feat: a notice on sites that need DRM

Nothing protected by Widevine plays yet (S-270), so Netflix and the like load
and then fail. A tab that commits a page on a short built-in list of sites now
shows a bar that says so, with Open in Safari on the Mac and Open in Edge on
Windows. The page is not blocked. The bar comes once per tab per site. "Don't
show again" remembers the site in stedding.drm_notice.dismissed_sites, and
Settings > Stedding lists those sites, each with a remove button
(docs/features/drm-notice.md Dn1-Dn12; settings T56).

A private window keeps its answer in its own preferences, in memory. A peek
over the page has no bar until it becomes a tab. TabFeatures attaches the
helper and carries its once across a tab going to sleep. A bar's link now sits
on the bar's line with a gap from the button, on every bar (toolbar T54).

The Windows half of the button has not been built.

Why: the owner's decision of 2026-11-05 (BACKLOG S-421): do not block these
sites; say why their video fails and offer a browser that plays it.

Removable when: Widevine plays in Stedding (BACKLOG S-270).
